<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>HG_Hound</defName>
    <label>helghan shepherd</label>
    <devNote>helghan shepherd</devNote>
    <description>Descended from German Shepherds, the helghast's closest thing to a domestic breed is this tragic creature. Originally, during the exodus from Vekta, most helghast families were forced to abandon or euthanize their pets, Terran imperial refugee mass-lifters only had capacity for so many beings - animals included, and the Helghan Corporation made the hard choice to cull all non-essential lifestock. But even then, mans best friend proved too steadfast an ally in those days to abandon wholesale, The logic went that the German Shepherd- a common choice for guard dogs and personal favorite of many helghast executives, would be an admirable choice for all sorts of important jobs, and so they were retained during resettlement.\n\nLike everything else, the Helghast corporation assumed that the planet side habitation facilities would shield the breeds from the adverse effects of the planet, They were wrong. In the ensuing humanitarian crisis, large kennels of hounds were released to the wild plains outside of Pyrrhus. A few were test subjects intended to see how the creatures adapted to the environment with aggressive gene-therapy to try and ensure their survival. In other cases, the kennel masters were simply victims of the cancers and lung conditions sweeping the helghan populace at the time. Either way, the 'Neo-Molossian' was borne in that hostile, irradiated outback.\n\nLiving nasty, brutish, short lives, the Helghan Shepherd grows fast and vicious, Its once beautiful coat has been largely replaced with trim, drab hairs to shed excess heat during the harsh summer months. They prey on scarce helghan fauna and flora, lingering at the edge of Helghast civilization, and battling the native 'corpse beetles' over carrion. In the ashes of the old regime, the new Helghan dictatorship saw a kindred spirit in the spiteful, brutal hound, In the decades since the regime rose from the ashes, most Neo-Molossians were captured and repurposed as interrogation tools, 'police dogs', war hounds, and weapons of terror and suppression. Many a political prisoner has been fed to the hounds, What was once a symbol of pride and duty has become warped into a fearsome weapon.\n\nSadly, the dogs heightened aggression is due to their medical conditions; even with rebreather support and good living conditions, they are in constant pain from muscle growths, rogue bone formations tearing at their internal muscles, and mutations- including a form of canine gigantism. After six years, Helghan Shepherds are considered 'old' and show lowered aggression, increased tiredness, and early signs of organ failure. Most civilian owners brave enough to raise them euthanize their faithful hounds rather than watch these once proud titans rip themselves apart. The regime considers these adaptations acceptable, because they are the very things which make the dogs quick to breed, grow, and fight.</description>
